\section{Vulnerability Scoring}
\label{sec:vulnerability-scoring}

When a Cyber Hygiene Vulnerability Scanning (CyHy VS) finding includes a Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures
(CVE) identifier, the severity rating is determined using the following order of sources:
\begin{itemize}
  	\setlength{\parskip}{0pt}  % Minimize vertical spacing
  	\setlength{\itemsep}{1pt}  % Minimize vertical spacing
	\item \href{https://cve.org/}{CVE.org} - Primary source
	\item National Vulnerability Database (NVD) - CVSS v3.1, then CVSS v3.0
	\item CVSS v2.0 - Used only if no v3 score is available, with one exception:
		  a base score of 10.0 will be rated as Critical
	\item Tenable Nessus score
\end{itemize}

